IO-54: start the pump's minimum flow at its first running flow

stats_open() sets PumpStats[].minFlow to 0 and stats_updateLinkStats()
lowers it with MIN(minFlow, q) for every step the pump runs, so it can
never rise above 0 and the Pumping Summary's Min Flow column (and
swmm_getPumpStats().minFlow) is always 0. Take the first running flow as
the starting value; a pump that never runs still reports 0.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-54_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/stats.c b/src/legacy/engine/stats.c
index 6d38f70..d8ee636 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/stats.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/stats.c
@@ -669,6 +669,7 @@ void stats_updateLinkStats(int j, double tStep, DateTime aDate)
         if ( q > MIN_RUNOFF_FLOW )
         {
             k = Link[j].subIndex;
+            if ( PumpStats[k].totalPeriods == 0 ) PumpStats[k].minFlow = q;
             PumpStats[k].minFlow = MIN(PumpStats[k].minFlow, q);
             PumpStats[k].maxFlow = LinkStats[j].maxFlow;
             PumpStats[k].avgFlow += q;
